                                    <h1>Diwali Marketing Playbook for D2C Brands (India) 2026-2027</h1>
                                    <p>Diwali (October-November) drives 25-40% of annual revenue for many Indian D2C brands. The extended festive period (Navratri → Dussehra → Karwa Chauth → Dhanteras → Diwali → Bhai Dooj) creates 4-6 weeks of peak activity. Here is the complete playbook based on running festive campaigns for 100+ Indian D2C brands.</p>
                                    <h2>Diwali Timeline: Extended Festive Period</h2>
                                    <p><strong>Navratri (9-10 days, late Sep / early Oct):</strong> traditional dress + gold gifting + preparation content.<br><strong>Dussehra:</strong> Vijayadashami + traditional purchases.<br><strong>Karwa Chauth:</strong> jewelry + fashion peaks.<br><strong>Dhanteras (2 days before Diwali):</strong> jewelry + electronics + home gold peak.<br><strong>Diwali:</strong> peak gifting + home + fashion + F&amp;B.<br><strong>Bhai Dooj:</strong> sibling gifting + jewelry.<br><strong>Post-Diwali sale extension:</strong> 3-5 days follow-through.<br><strong>Total peak period:</strong> 4-6 weeks.</p>
                                    <h2>Planning Timeline</h2>
                                    <p><strong>12-16 weeks before Diwali:</strong> creative + inventory + budget planning.<br><strong>8-10 weeks before:</strong> shoot creative + creator commitments + PR outreach.<br><strong>4-6 weeks before:</strong> pre-festive teaser campaigns.<br><strong>2-4 weeks before:</strong> full campaign launch.<br><strong>During peak:</strong> daily monitoring + creative rotation + inventory reallocation.<br><strong>Post-Diwali:</strong> follow-through sale + winners + retention flows.</p>
                                    <h2>Category-Specific Playbook</h2>
                                    <p><strong>Fashion:</strong> ethnic wear + occasion collections launch 4-6 weeks pre-Diwali. Wedding-season overlap (Nov-Feb).<br><strong>Beauty + skincare:</strong> Diwali gift kits + festive makeup collections + at-home ritual content.<br><strong>Jewelry:</strong> Dhanteras + Diwali peak — gold buying tradition drives massive volume.<br><strong>Consumer electronics:</strong> Diwali sale + Big Billion Days / Great Indian Sale drive volume.<br><strong>Home + decor:</strong> Diwali cleaning + decor + gifting.<br><strong>F&amp;B:</strong> sweets + festive hampers + corporate gifting.<br><strong>Corporate gifting:</strong> 40-60% of B2B annual revenue concentrated in Sep-Nov.</p>
                                    <h2>Ad Budget Concentration</h2>
                                    <p>Diwali CPM inflation in India: 40-80% during Big Billion Days / Great Indian Sale + Dhanteras + Diwali week.<br><strong>Recommended allocation:</strong> pre-festive (weeks 8-12): 10%. Festive buildup (weeks 4-8): 20-25%. Peak (Dhanteras + Diwali week): 40-50%. Post-Diwali: 15-25%.<br>Concentrate spend during actual purchase windows.</p>
                                    <h2>Creative Themes That Work</h2>
                                    <p>Family + celebration + togetherness themes. Traditional-modern blend. Gifting language. Nostalgia + family memories. Regional Diwali variations (North vs South vs East vs West Indian celebrations differ).<br>Regional-language content in Hindi + Tamil + Telugu + Kannada + Bengali + Marathi + Gujarati outperforms English-only for Diwali campaigns.</p>
                                    <h2>Corporate Gifting Strategy</h2>
                                    <p>Corporate Diwali gifting drives 30-50% of B2B revenue for gifting-oriented brands. Timeline: outreach in July-August. Client-tailored offering catalogs in September. Delivery in October (2-4 weeks before Diwali). Client teams need gifts delivered before Diwali holiday period.</p>

